index 4479b53..ed6a30e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,35 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkey UI integration
+
+Sign-in and sign-up offer password or WebAuthn passkey flows. `/devtools-times/account`
+provides passkey creation, renaming, removal, and identity confirmation. No credentials
+or authentication state are stored in localStorage. The UI displays API failures
+rather than simulating successful authentication.
+
+Set `PUBLIC_AUTH_API_URL` to the authentication API base (defaults to the existing
+Times API). Requests include cookies. Cross-origin hosting requires explicit CORS
+origins, credentials support, and secure cookies with the appropriate SameSite policy.
+The external authentication service must implement this contract; its implementation
+is outside this repository:
+
+- `POST /login`, `/register`: existing `{ username, password }` requests; login must establish a session.
+- `GET /passkeys`: authenticated `{ passkeys: [{ id, name, createdAt, lastUsedAt?, current? }] }`.
+- `POST /passkeys/register/options`: `{ username? }` → `{ options, challengeId }`. With a username, begin account registration; without one, require an authenticated session and recent verification. Options use base64url for binary values.
+- `POST /passkeys/register/verify`: `{ challengeId, credential, name }` → successful registration and session. Do not create the account until the credential is verified.
+- `POST /passkeys/authenticate/options`: `{ purpose: "signin" | "reauthenticate", username? }` → `{ options, challengeId }`. Omit `allowCredentials` for discoverable sign-in; bind reauthentication to the current account.
+- `POST /passkeys/authenticate/verify`: `{ purpose, challengeId, credential }` → establish a sign-in session, or return `{ reauthenticationToken }` for recent identity confirmation.
+- `POST /reauthenticate`: `{ password }` → `{ reauthenticationToken }` for the current account.
+- `POST /passkeys/authorize-registration`: `{ reauthenticationToken }` → authorize one registration ceremony in the current server session.
+- `PATCH /passkeys/:id`: `{ name, reauthenticationToken }`; `DELETE /passkeys/:id`: `{ reauthenticationToken }`. Enforce ownership, recent verification, and recovery access before removal. Both may return 204.
+
+The service must generate unpredictable, expiring, single-use challenges; verify
+expected origin, RP ID, signature, user verification, and credential ownership;
+store public keys and counters; enforce rate limits and CSRF protection; rotate
+sessions at sign-in; and bind short-lived reauthentication proofs to the account
+and protected operation. Never trust a client claim of successful verification.
+WebAuthn requires HTTPS (or localhost). Cancelled authenticator prompts leave
+account state unchanged. Registration uses discoverable credentials and requires
+user verification; older browsers use explicit base64url conversion.
